    "explain": "No console guard fails the test on a logged error, so a React warning or a caught exception logged to `console.error` scrolls past under a green run. Add a `console.error`/`console.warn` spy whose implementation throws, or a fail-on-console package, in the setup file, so a logged error is a failing test.",
